course: dictionary
lesson: 15395
title: An old-fashioned word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context helps you work out a word you do not know. Read the words around it and look for clues. «The spinster lived alone in a small cottage at the edge of the village, and she had never married.» The words never married tell you that a spinster is a woman who has not married.
explain: Spinster is an old-fashioned word for a woman who has never married, usually an older one. Today people often say «a single woman» or «unmarried» instead. Spinster can sound unkind, because in the past it was used to mock women who did not marry.
explain: Long ago, a spinster could also be a woman whose job was spinning thread. «The spinster sat by the fire, turning wool into thread.» Wool and thread are the clues here, so this meaning fits the sentence. Always check which meaning makes sense.
fact: A spinster is a woman who has never married, usually an older one.
fact: «Spinster» is an old-fashioned word, and it can sound unkind.
fact: Long ago, a spinster was also a woman whose job was spinning thread.
fact: In old legal papers, «spinster» was the word for an unmarried woman.
fact: The male word «bachelor» is still used more freely than «spinster».
exercise: «The spinster sat by the fire, turning wool into thread.» What did the spinster do? | Painted the kitchen wall | *Spun thread from wool | Cooked a huge dinner | Ran a race across the field
exercise: «The spinster lived alone in a small cottage, and she had never married.» What is a spinster? | A man who sails boats | A bell that rings at noon | *A woman who has never married | A horse that runs very fast
exercise: Mum says a modern way to say spinster is a different phrase. Which one is it? | A tall tree | *A single woman | A loud bell | A red bicycle
test: Why can the word spinster sound unkind? | It is only used for children | *It was used to mock women who did not marry | It is a word for a bird | It means a very happy person
test: «In the old legal paper, the word spinster was written for the woman's name.» What did spinster mean in that paper? | A queen | *An unmarried woman | A ship's captain | A farmer's cow
exam: Which male word is still used more freely than spinster? | *bachelor | hermit | baker
